## an4.184
an4.184:1.1 | S: Then the brahmin Jānussoṇi went up to the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. | T: Then Jānussoṇi the brahman went to the Blessed One and, on arrival, exchanged courteous greetings with him.
an4.184:1.2 | S: When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to the Buddha: | T: After an exchange of friendly greetings & courtesies, he sat to one side. As he was sitting there he said to the Blessed One:
an4.184:2.1 | S: “Worthy Gotama, this is my doctrine and view: | T: “I am of the view & opinion
an4.184:2.2 | S: ‘All those liable to death are frightened and terrified of death.’” | T: that there is no one who, subject to death, is not afraid or in terror of death.”
an4.184:2.3 | S: “Brahmin, some of those liable to death are frightened and terrified of death. | T: (The Blessed One said:) “Brahman, there are those who, subject to death, are afraid & in terror of death.
an4.184:2.4 | S: But some of those liable to death are not frightened and terrified of death. | T: And there are those who, subject to death, are not afraid or in terror of death.
an4.184:3.1 | S: Who are those frightened of death? | T: “And who is the person who, subject to death, is afraid & in terror of death?
an4.184:3.2 | S: It’s someone who isn’t free of greed, desire, fondness, thirst, passion, and craving for sensual pleasures. | T: There is the case of the person who has not abandoned passion, desire, fondness, thirst, fever, & craving for sensuality.
an4.184:3.3 | S: When they fall seriously ill, | T: Then he comes down with a serious disease. As he comes down with a serious disease,
an4.184:3.4 | S: they think: | T: the thought occurs to him,
an4.184:3.5 | S: ‘The sensual pleasures that I love so much will leave me, and I’ll leave them.’ | T: ‘O, those beloved sensual pleasures will be taken from me, and I will be taken from them!’
an4.184:3.6 | S: They sorrow and wail and lament, beating their breast and falling into confusion. | T: He grieves & is tormented, weeps, beats his breast, & grows delirious.
an4.184:3.7 | S: This is someone who is frightened of death. | T: This is a person who, subject to death, is afraid & in terror of death.
an4.184:4.1 | S: Furthermore, it’s someone who isn’t free of greed, desire, fondness, thirst, passion, and craving for the body. | T: “Then there is the case of the person who has not abandoned passion, desire, fondness, thirst, fever, & craving for the body.
an4.184:4.2 | S: When they fall seriously ill, | T: Then he comes down with a serious disease. As he comes down with a serious disease,
an4.184:4.3 | S: they think: | T: the thought occurs to him,
an4.184:4.4 | S: ‘This body that I love so much will leave me, and I’ll leave it.’ | T: ‘O, my beloved body will be taken from me, and I will be taken from my body!’
an4.184:4.5 | S: They sorrow and wail and lament, beating their breast and falling into confusion. | T: He grieves & is tormented, weeps, beats his breast, & grows delirious.
an4.184:4.6 | S: This, too, is someone who is frightened of death. | T: This, too, is a person who, subject to death, is afraid & in terror of death.
an4.184:5.1 | S: Furthermore, it’s someone who hasn’t done good and skillful things that keep them safe, but has done bad things, violence and sin. | T: “Then there is the case of the person who has not done what is good, has not done what is skillful, has not given protection to those in fear, and instead has done what is evil, savage, & cruel.
an4.184:5.2 | S: When they fall seriously ill, | T: Then he comes down with a serious disease. As he comes down with a serious disease,
an4.184:5.3 | S: they think: | T: the thought occurs to him,
an4.184:5.4 | S: ‘Well, I haven’t done good and skillful things that keep me safe. | T: ‘I have not done what is good, have not done what is skillful, have not given protection to those in fear,
an4.184:5.5 | S: And I have done bad things, violence and sin. | T: and instead have done what is evil, savage, & cruel.
an4.184:5.6 | S: When I depart, I’ll go to the place where people who’ve done such things go.’ | T: To the extent that there is a destination for those who have not done what is good, have not done what is skillful, have not given protection to those in fear, and instead have done what is evil, savage, & cruel, that’s where I’m headed after death.’
an4.184:5.7 | S: They sorrow and wail and lament, beating their breast and falling into confusion. | T: He grieves & is tormented, weeps, beats his breast, & grows delirious.
an4.184:5.8 | S: This, too, is someone who is frightened of death. | T: This, too, is a person who, subject to death, is afraid & in terror of death.
an4.184:6.1 | S: Furthermore, it’s someone who’s doubtful, uncertain, and undecided about the true teaching. | T: “Then there is the case of the person in doubt & perplexity, who has not arrived at certainty with regard to the True Dhamma.
an4.184:6.2 | S: When they fall seriously ill, | T: Then he comes down with a serious disease. As he comes down with a serious disease,
an4.184:6.3 | S: they think: | T: the thought occurs to him,
an4.184:6.4 | S: ‘I’m doubtful, uncertain, and undecided about the true teaching.’ | T: ‘How doubtful & perplexed I am! I have not arrived at any certainty with regard to the True Dhamma!’
an4.184:6.5 | S: They sorrow and wail and lament, beating their breast and falling into confusion. | T: He grieves & is tormented, weeps, beats his breast, & grows delirious.
an4.184:6.6 | S: This, too, is someone who is frightened of death. | T: This, too, is a person who, subject to death, is afraid & in terror of death.
an4.184:6.7 | S: These are the four individuals liable to death who are frightened and terrified of death. | T: “These, brahman, are four people who, subject to death, are afraid & in terror of death.
an4.184:7.1 | S: Who are those not frightened of death? | T: “And who is the person who, subject to death, is not afraid or in terror of death?
an4.184:7.2 | S: It’s someone who is rid of greed, desire, fondness, thirst, passion, and craving for sensual pleasures. | T: “There is the case of the person who has abandoned passion, desire, fondness, thirst, fever, & craving for sensuality.
an4.184:7.3 | S: When they fall seriously ill, | T: Then he comes down with a serious disease. As he comes down with a serious disease,
an4.184:7.4 | S: they don’t think: | T: the thought doesn’t occur to him,
an4.184:7.5 | S: ‘The sensual pleasures that I love so much will leave me, and I’ll leave them.’ | T: ‘O, those beloved sensual pleasures will be taken from me, and I will be taken from them!’
an4.184:7.6 | S: They don’t sorrow and wail and lament, beating their breast and falling into confusion. | T: He doesn’t grieve, isn’t tormented; doesn’t weep, beat his breast, or grow delirious.
an4.184:7.7 | S: This is someone who’s not frightened of death. | T: This is a person who, subject to death, is not afraid or in terror of death.
an4.184:8.1 | S: Furthermore, it’s someone who is rid of greed, desire, fondness, thirst, passion, and craving for the body. | T: “Then there is the case of the person who has abandoned passion, desire, fondness, thirst, fever, & craving for the body.
